---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
---

<BaseLayout title="About - Yonatan N. Degefu" description="How Yonatan N. Degefu moved from biology to quantitative research.">
  <div class="about-container">
    <p class="eyebrow page-kicker">What motivates me</p>
    <h1>About Me</h1>

    <section class="bio-section">
      <p>
        I trained primarily as a biologist, and along the way I was drawn to using math and data to
        test biological hypotheses. My research began with how plants defend themselves against
        mites, then moved to regulatory T cells, where I built my first image-analysis pipelines, then
        to drug combinations for tuberculosis, and now to cancer.
      </p>
      <p>
        Living systems have too many interacting parts to reason about by intuition alone. I build
        models to check whether a proposed mechanism can explain what we measure, and to predict what
        should happen in experiments we haven’t run yet. I pay closest attention when a model and an
        experiment disagree, because that’s often where there is something new to learn.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the projects and methods I’ve worked on so far, see
        my <a href={withBase('/research/')}>research</a> and <a href={withBase('/cv/')}>CV</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="bio-section" aria-labelledby="beyond-heading">
      <h2 id="beyond-heading">Beyond research</h2>
      <p>
        I enjoy spending time outdoors and cooking international cuisines. I also care about mentoring
        and service. I’ve guided summer undergraduate researchers from their first training to
        presenting at the Biomedical Engineering Society annual meeting, and I volunteer in
        outreach programs and with community organizations.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
